STLport container integration

include/stlport-containers/ contains the unmodified STLport 4.5.3 headers
selected by compiler dependency scans of the accepted instantiations.
Copyright/permission notices remain in each file. The archive and every
selected file are pinned in config/GR8E69/stlport-source.json.

include/stlport-runtime/ supplies this project's configuration and the native
new/exception declarations from GCC 2.95.2 (Free Software Foundation copyright).
The new header leaves bad_alloc::what declared out of line instead of defining
its unused inline body. No accepted object instantiates or references it.
The exception header is unchanged. GNU GPL v2 is supplied as COPYING.GCC;
no additional header-specific licensing exception is asserted.

src/stlport/containers/ contains project-written explicit instantiations using
original symbol types. Game pointees stay forward-declared. These files do not
claim original source-file boundaries, game layouts or the original compiler
and library releases. All retained algorithm bodies come from STLport.

AI assisted the symbol inventory, instantiation selection, configuration,
integration and byte verification. See docs/STLport.md.
